=====================================================
PHASE 9 — AUTONOMOUS IMPROVEMENT ENGINE
=====================================================

This is another PRIMARY PRODUCT FEATURE.

After research is completed, analyse which properties can improve and why.

Potential diagnoses:
- Weak information coefficient
- Unstable performance across regimes
- Excessive turnover
- High transaction costs
- Overfitting
- Poor risk-adjusted returns
- Excessive drawdowns
- Factor redundancy
- Tail sensitivity
- Limited investment capacity
- High computational cost
- Data-quality limitations
- Model instability
- Uncertain statistical significance

For every identified weakness generate an Improvement Card containing:

1. Property being improved
2. Baseline value
3. Relevant uncertainty
4. Likely causal explanation or testable hypothesis
5. Supporting evidence
6. Proposed modification
7. Theoretical justification
8. Expected direction of improvement
9. Required data and resources
10. Experimental protocol
11. Success criteria
12. Rejection criteria
13. Risks and possible regressions
14. Implementation complexity
15. Final observed outcome

Do not fabricate numerical forecasts of improvement.

Treat unverified predictions as hypotheses.

Rank recommendations according to evidence strength, expected value, implementation cost and risk.

Implement an improvement lifecycle:
PROPOSED → APPROVED → RUNNING → EVALUATED → ACCEPTED/REJECTED.

Compare accepted improvements to the original baseline using identical evaluation assumptions.

Expose an interactive before/after comparison.

Record unsuccessful improvements and reasons for rejection.

Avoid repeatedly tuning on the same test set.

Do not deploy newly generated strategy code without sandboxed execution, tests and an explicit approval policy.

