DEFINITION OF DONE
=====================================================

AlphaForge is publication-quality only when:

1. It can execute a complete research workflow on actual or clearly labelled demonstration data.
2. The backtesting engine has passed correctness tests.
3. Research results are reproducible from stored configurations.
4. The website is deployed and works across supported devices.
5. Interactive controls perform real actions.
6. A research report can be generated from genuine results.
7. The improvement engine can diagnose a weakness and evaluate a proposed change.
8. All outputs expose evidence, assumptions and limitations.
9. GitHub Actions successfully execute configured workflows.
10. A new developer can restore the application without the original Gemini session.
11. The repository contains the required documentation.
12. No secrets are committed.
13. The system can distinguish exploratory from validated research.
14. The technical claims withstand independent review.
15. The live product is demonstrable to a quantitative finance interviewer.

FINAL DIRECTIVE

Begin immediately with repository reconnaissance and Phase 0.

Then implement M1 as an end-to-end working product rather than generating a large amount of disconnected scaffolding.

Continue through the defined milestones as permitted by the environment, performing real actions, tests and Git operations.

If interrupted, persist the precise state and next steps.

The mission is not to produce plausible code. It is to create an elegant, mathematically rigorous, reproducible, deployable and genuinely functional quantitative research platform.
